WEBVTT

00:00.320 --> 00:02.340
- [Instructor] So let's
see if we can try to factor

00:02.340 --> 00:05.820
the following expression completely.

00:05.820 --> 00:07.130
So factor this completely,

00:07.130 --> 00:09.143
pause the video and have a go at that.

00:10.160 --> 00:12.200
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:12.200 --> 00:14.410
So the way that I like to think about it,

00:14.410 --> 00:17.240
I first try to see is
there any common factor

00:17.240 --> 00:19.820
to all the terms, and I
try to find the greatest

00:19.820 --> 00:20.900
of the common factor,

00:20.900 --> 00:23.500
possible common factors
to all of the terms.

00:23.500 --> 00:26.410
So let's see, they're
all divisible by two,

00:26.410 --> 00:27.960
so two would be a common factor,

00:27.960 --> 00:30.270
but let's see, they're
also all divisible by four,

00:30.270 --> 00:33.030
four is divisible by four,
eight is divisible by four,

00:33.030 --> 00:34.780
12 is divisible by four,

00:34.780 --> 00:37.390
and that looks like the
greatest common factor.

00:37.390 --> 00:38.820
They're not all divisible by x,

00:38.820 --> 00:40.540
so I can't throw an x in there.

00:40.540 --> 00:42.970
So what I wanna do is factor out a four.

00:42.970 --> 00:46.290
So I could re-write this as four times,

00:46.290 --> 00:48.320
now what would it be, four times what?

00:48.320 --> 00:51.150
Well if I factor a four
out of four x squared,

00:51.150 --> 00:53.910
I'm just going to be
left with an x squared.

00:53.910 --> 00:57.530
If I factor a four out
of negative eight x,

00:57.530 --> 01:00.420
negative eight x divided
by four is negative two,

01:00.420 --> 01:03.000
so I'm going to have negative two x.

01:03.000 --> 01:08.000
And if I factor a four out of negative 12,

01:08.070 --> 01:12.520
negative 12 divided by
four is negative three.

01:12.520 --> 01:14.200
Now am I done factoring?

01:14.200 --> 01:16.310
Well it looks like I
could factor this thing

01:16.310 --> 01:17.500
a little bit more.

01:17.500 --> 01:21.200
Can I think of two numbers
that add up to negative two,

01:21.200 --> 01:23.510
and when I multiply it
I get negative three,

01:23.510 --> 01:25.320
since when I multiply
I get a negative value,

01:25.320 --> 01:26.741
one of the 'em is going to be positive

01:26.741 --> 01:27.770
and one of 'em is going to be negative.

01:27.770 --> 01:29.350
I can think about it this way.

01:29.350 --> 01:32.050
A plus B is equal to negative two,

01:32.050 --> 01:35.070
A times B needs to be
equal to negative three.

01:35.070 --> 01:37.600
So let's see, A could be
equal to negative three

01:37.600 --> 01:39.670
and B could be equal to one

01:39.670 --> 01:43.450
because negative three
plus one is negative two,

01:43.450 --> 01:46.470
and negative three times
one is negative three.

01:46.470 --> 01:48.160
So I could re-write all of this

01:48.160 --> 01:53.160
as four times x plus negative three,

01:53.670 --> 01:56.090
or I could just write
that as x minus three,

01:56.090 --> 02:00.430
times x plus one, x plus one.

02:00.430 --> 02:05.280
And now I have actually
factored this completely.

02:05.280 --> 02:07.773
Let's do another example.

02:09.300 --> 02:12.200
So let's say that we had the expression

02:12.200 --> 02:17.200
negative three x squared
plus 21 x minus 30.

02:17.760 --> 02:21.370
Pause the video and see if you
can factor this completely.

02:21.370 --> 02:22.760
All right now let's do this together.

02:22.760 --> 02:24.830
So what would be the
greatest common factor?

02:24.830 --> 02:28.010
So let's see, they're
all divisible by three,

02:28.010 --> 02:29.690
so you could factor out a three.

02:29.690 --> 02:31.470
Let's see what happens if
you factor out a three.

02:31.470 --> 02:34.120
This is the same thing as three times,

02:34.120 --> 02:35.600
well negative three x squared divided

02:35.600 --> 02:38.110
by three is negative x squared,

02:38.110 --> 02:41.810
21 x divided by three is
seven x, so plus seven x,

02:41.810 --> 02:45.520
and then negative 30 divided
by three is negative 10.

02:45.520 --> 02:46.930
You could do it this way,

02:46.930 --> 02:49.970
but having this negative
out on the x squared term

02:49.970 --> 02:51.560
still makes it a little bit confusing

02:51.560 --> 02:53.240
on how you would factor this further.

02:53.240 --> 02:54.610
You can do it, but it still takes

02:54.610 --> 02:57.120
a little bit more of a mental load.

02:57.120 --> 02:58.590
So instead of just factoring out a three,

02:58.590 --> 03:00.120
let's factor out a negative three.

03:00.120 --> 03:01.050
So we could write it this way.

03:01.050 --> 03:04.070
If we factor out a negative
three, what does that become?

03:04.070 --> 03:06.090
Well then if you factor
out a negative three out

03:06.090 --> 03:08.730
of this term, you're just
left with an x squared.

03:08.730 --> 03:11.520
If you factor out a negative
three from this term,

03:11.520 --> 03:15.000
21 divided by negative
three is negative seven x.

03:15.000 --> 03:18.990
And if you factor out a negative
three out of negative 30,

03:18.990 --> 03:22.820
you're left with a
positive 10, positive 10.

03:22.820 --> 03:25.370
And now let's see if we
can factor this thing

03:25.370 --> 03:26.470
a little bit more.

03:26.470 --> 03:30.110
Can I think of two numbers
where if I were to add them

03:30.110 --> 03:32.320
I get to negative seven,

03:32.320 --> 03:35.790
and if I were to multiply
them, I get to 10?

03:35.790 --> 03:37.890
And let's see, they'd
have to have the same sign

03:37.890 --> 03:39.660
'cause their product is positive.

03:39.660 --> 03:42.580
So let's see A could be
equal to negative five,

03:42.580 --> 03:45.230
and then B is equal to negative two.

03:45.230 --> 03:47.490
So I can re-write this
whole thing as equal

03:47.490 --> 03:50.430
to negative three times
x plus negative five,

03:50.430 --> 03:52.400
which is the same thing as x minus five,

03:52.400 --> 03:53.910
times x plus negative two,

03:53.910 --> 03:56.810
which is the same thing as x minus two.

03:56.810 --> 03:59.233
And now we have factored completely.
